From 8fed950446170ad94ac3b17854a2015b34083e02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mira (mira/mira)" <hey2missmira@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 08:50:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] (be) ck-phdr-unwind libunwind capture_into_slot

Add the variant TU `be/src/service/http/action/print_stack_ck_phdr_unwind.cpp`. The handler-side hook copies the interrupted thread's `ucontext_t` into a libunwind context, calls `unw_init_local2` with `UNW_INIT_SIGNAL_FRAME`, and walks via `unw_get_reg(UNW_REG_IP)` + `unw_step` up to `kMaxSignalFrames`. A `hasPHDRCache()` gate refuses to unwind if patch 2's `updatePHDRCache()` never ran.

TSan exception: `be/src/common/phdr_cache.cpp` compile-guards the override off when `THREAD_SANITIZER` is defined (TSan installs its own `dl_iterate_phdr` interceptor and refuses a user override), so `hasPHDRCache()` is always false in a TSan build. The defense-in-depth rationale (avoid the loader lock from the signal handler) is moot under TSan, which serializes loader access through its runtime and is debug-only. The gate is therefore `#if !defined(THREAD_SANITIZER)` so the test case `BestEffortFrameObserved` exercises real frames under TSan instead of degrading to CaptureFailed.

`UNW_LOCAL_ONLY` is defined before `<libunwind.h>` so the include resolves to the local-only `_ULx86_64_*` symbols the Doris libunwind archive exports. `be/src/service/CMakeLists.txt` globs `*.cpp` recursively, so the new TU is picked up without a CMakeLists edit.

Spec: docs/architecture.md "Layer 3d"; docs/design/ck.md "Decisions", "Shape", "Workflow".

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
